  "review_notes": {
    "checks": "All original check sites retained, with native expected fixture values and explicit zero legacy PoW accessor contract. Four additional check sites strengthen truncation, ProcessBlock acceptance and lookup-read validity.",
    "lookup_cache": "Only fixed-chain transaction lookup reads are memoized. All explicit full-chain reads, validation/reindex/undo/script/UTXO assertions and post-file-deletion error checks remain uncached.",
    "fixtures": "Frozen independently verified one-mainnet/206-regtest real-proof snapshot; current Python structure checks and header rendering match. Earlier scalar/public Rust proof evidence retained without unnecessary rerun.",
    "functional_299_amendment": "Functional-only native regtest height299 commitment amendment, independently reconstructed from both scenario chains and all snapshot bytes. Bitcoin preprocessed translation unit byte-identical; native preprocessed delta consists only of the two299hash literals. Evidence: artifacts/functional-green-20261009/native-assumeutxo-preprocessing-review.json and native-assumeutxo-vectors.json. All mainnet/testnet/signet/height110/height200 parameters and proof fixture bytes unchanged."
  },
  "signet_calibration_initialization_review": "Native Signet initializes fPoCXLowCapacityCalibration=false, matching its existing normal-capacity genesis. Independently reproduced wrong regtest target before fix; Bitcoin preprocessed translation unit identical; every existing mainnet/regtest field and fixture byte unchanged. artifacts/functional-green-20261009/signet-calibration-preprocessing-review.json",
  "ci_baseline_review": "Add an explicit --bitcoin mode to the existing strict kernel runner/verifier. It requires ENABLE_POCX=OFF and snapshots original fixtures plus shared production sources. Both modes still rebuild, check current hashes, require all16 original runtime/Boost cases and exactly one successful non-skipped CTest wrapper. PoCX source, case, fixture, assertion and execution-input requirements remain unchanged. Binary names support native Windows .exe builds.",
  "regtest_kernel_permission_review": "Extract unchanged synthetic quality calculation into wallet/global-free regtest proof.cpp; an explicit default-false consensus permission is enabled only in CRegTestParams. CheckBlockHeader and header batching use passed context parameters in daemon and kernel. Real-proof validation, signatures, compression and future-time checks remain required; production networks retain synthetic rejection. Original Bitcoin preprocessing and kernel baseline are checked separately.",
  "sanitizer_timeout_review": "Positive explicit CTest timeout; default900seconds retained, inherited ASan uses2400seconds. All16cases, assertion proof, source/build attestations and failure/skip rejection are unchanged."
}
